; Seatbelt rules and entitlements for Serein.app itself, on top of App Sandbox. App Sandbox
; already confines it to its container and to what the user picks in open/save panels or drags
; in; these rules take away what the app never does. Tools/build-app.sh turns this file into
; the app's entitlements (Tools/sbpl-entitlements.sh): `;!` lines are entitlements, rules go in
; com.apple.security.temporary-exception.sbpl. Every deny has a match-everything filter (App
; Sandbox's filtered allows win over unfiltered denies). The app checks at start-up that the
; sandbox is in force and exits otherwise.
;
; Signal's servers (chat, storage, CDN, SFU), contacts discovery. (Calls run in SignalCalling.xpc.)
;! com.apple.security.network.client
; Video calls: the app captures the camera and hands the frames to SignalCalling.xpc.
;! com.apple.security.device.camera
; The microphone is not the app's: calls record in SignalCalling.xpc, voice notes in
; SignalVoiceNoteEncoder.xpc. macOS asks the user for those services on the app's behalf, and
; only for an app that carries this entitlement, so it stays; the rule below takes the
; microphone itself away from the app (its input is silence).
;! com.apple.security.device.audio-input
(deny device-microphone)
; Attachments, exports and saves the user picks (open/save panels, drag and drop).
;! com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write
; The crash-report dialog reads macOS's reports for this app (read-only).
;!+ com.apple.security.temporary-exception.files.home-relative-path.read-only /Library/Logs/DiagnosticReports/
;
; No other programs, no children (links open through Launch Services, not a process).
(deny process-exec* (subpath "/"))
(deny process-fork)
; No scripting other apps, no changing kernel state, no signalling other processes.
(deny appleevent-send)
(deny sysctl-write)
(deny signal (target others))
